"]},{"name":"schedulePrint","subType":"yesNoReference","type":"REFERENCE","values":["Y"]},{"name":"gradingScale","subType":"gradingScaleRef","type":"REFERENCE","values":["GRD"]},{"name":"dutchNameShort","type":"STRING","values":["Speech sounds of the World TEN"]}],"year":{"code":"2026-2027","id":"2261","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"2026-2027"},{"language":"NL","value":"2026-2027"}],"uid":"07254806-916f-4cca-82a0-2e69a4a95e9f"}},"required":true,"values":[{"name":"evaluate","subType":"yesNoReference","type":"REFERENCE","values":["Y"]}],"weighting":1.00}],"capacity":{"optimum":45.00},"code":"5511VE005Y","credits":{"maximum":5.00,"minimum":5.00,"optimum":5.00},"descriptions":[{"language":"EN","text":"Students learn to produce, recognize, transcribe, and analyze speech sounds during the lectures and the practice sessions. They will be confronted with speech sounds they are familiar with and with speech sounds they are less familiar with among consonants, vowels and tone.\n\nThe course consists of a one hour lecture (held twice, once in English, once in Dutch) followed by a one hour practice session where students learn how to produce the speech sounds. The course is supported by a custom-made digital course helping the students to recognize and to describe speech sounds.","type":{"code":"CO","id":"CO","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Description"},{"language":"NL","value":"Beschrijving"}],"uid":"9b0c3e97-ad09-42d7-a5bb-afdaf6f1877f"}},{"language":"EN","text":"No reading list.","type":{"code":"LI","id":"LI","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Reading list"},{"language":"NL","value":"Literatuurlijst"}],"uid":"fbd93a9e-ca99-4bcc-807f-39235bb6000b"}},{"language":"EN","text":"### Assessment and weighing\n\nWritten examination with closed and open questions: 60%\nDictation: 20%\nOral exam: 20%\nThe final mark for the course is established by determining the weighted average.","type":{"code":"TP","id":"TP","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Assessment method"},{"language":"NL","value":"Toetsing en weging"}],"uid":"687f9ba4-4330-4ab9-8536-be9ebd2c58c5"}},{"language":"EN","text":"Enrolment through [My Studymap](https://mijn.universiteitleiden.nl/login) is mandatory","type":{"code":"ENR","id":"ENR","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Registration"},{"language":"NL","value":"Inschrijven"}],"uid":"a77a2043-b0a9-450d-b780-1e90a4d3290c"}},{"language":"EN","text":"The course has four main objectives:\n\n* learning how to produce speech sounds;\n* learning how to recognize speech sounds;\n* learning to transcribe speech sounds according to the alphabet op the IPA (International Phonetics Association);\n* learning how to analyze and describe speech sounds.","type":{"code":"LO","id":"LO","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Course objectives"},{"language":"NL","value":"Leerdoelen"}],"uid":"b54eb210-96e8-490d-aadb-a70571a665d9"}},{"language":"EN","text":"There are no admission requirements.","type":{"code":"AR","id":"AR","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Admission requirements"},{"language":"NL","value":"Toegangseisen"}],"uid":"2c481598-5834-4422-a338-1eb346d6f52c"}},{"language":"EN","text":"For substantive questions; contact the lecturer listed in the right information bar\n\nFor questions related to the content of the course; please contact the lecturer; you can find their contact information by clicking on their name in the sidebar.\n\nFor questions regarding enrollment please contact the [Education Administration Office Reuvensplaats](https://www.organisatiegids.universiteitleiden.nl/faculteiten-en-instituten/geesteswetenschappen/faculteitsbureau/onderwijs--en-studentzaken/onderwijsadministraties/onderwijsadministratie-reuvensplaats) \nE-mail address Education Administration Office Reuvensplaats: osz-oa-reuvensplaats@hum.leidenuniv.nl\n\nFor questions regarding your study progress contact the study adviser: stuco-ba-linguistics@hum.leidenuniv.nl)","type":{"code":"CG","id":"CG","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Contact"},{"language":"NL","value":"Contact"}],"uid":"35f7e88a-830a-4877-b467-86a700954d19"}},{"language":"EN","text":"This course is parallel to the Dutch course *Klanken van de wereld*. If you are a native speaker fo Dutch; please register for *Klanken van de wereld.*\n\n","type":{"code":"RM","id":"RM","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Remarks"},{"language":"NL","value":"Opmerkingen"}],"uid":"c22c1513-23c4-41d5-aaf6-8ca4854ef2ea"}},{"language":"EN","text":"Lecture + practice sessions","type":{"code":"WV","id":"WV","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Teaching method"},{"language":"NL","value":"Onderwijsvorm"}],"uid":"26f0e596-e48d-46ff-8c8b-9b9688699943"}},{"language":"EN","text":"The timetables are available through My Timetable (see the button in the upper right corner).","type":{"code":"SC","id":"SC","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Schedule"},{"language":"NL","value":"Rooster"}],"uid":"939373d2-217d-4dde-9c37-6f6101f1ab75"}},{"language":"EN","text":"### Resit\n\nAll exams have the possibility of a resit.\n\n### Review and feedback\n\nHow and when an exam review will take place will be disclosed together with the publication of the exam results at the latest. If a student requests a review within 30 days after publication of the exam results, an exam review will have to be organized.","type":{"code":"RRD","id":"RRD","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Resit, review & feedback"},{"language":"NL","value":"Herkansing, inzage & nabespreking"}],"uid":"ef7be178-91d7-4f56-a40b-891976f3af1c"}}],"faculty":{"code":"FGW","id":"FGW","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Humanities"},{"language":"NL","value":"Geesteswetenschappen"}],"uid":"28c8aabb-f896-444f-895c-63ef88ba9307"},"id":"236304","key":102190,"methods":[{"method":{"category":"T","code":"5511VE005W","contactHours":13.00,"id":"236306","key":118613,"module":{"code":"5511VE005Y","id":"236304","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Speech sounds of the World"},{"language":"NL","value":"Speech sounds of the World"}],"uid":"bfd310e5-ac6a-440f-82f9-7b118f90